name issue_29_ulpfec_over_red
describe 5% random loss with NACK off, so video FEC runs (ShouldDisableRedAndUlpfec): ULPFEC over RED on the media SSRC, as libwebrtc sends it
# sm_compare runs 80 seeds here (#410). Ours on main f2d580c: video.freeze_total_ms 22602 on seeds 1-10, 23922 on
# 1-80 (sd 3647); video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 241 on 1-10, 224 on 1-80 (sd 38).
compare_seeds 80
duration 30s
nack off
at 0s capacity=2000kbps delay=40ms jitter=3ms loss=5% queue=300ms
# Issue #29 step 2: the session layer sends and receives ULPFEC (RFC 5109) over RED (RFC 2198).
# The FEC amount is libwebrtc's FecControllerDefault (#29 step 3, kFec: NACK is off). These lines
# check that FEC repairs loss end to end. Seeds 1-10: 124-172 packets recovered, residual loss
# 0.63-1.39 %, FEC 344-430 kbps (libwebrtc's mean 444) (4.94 % residual on seed 1 with `fec off`).
# With NACK off an unrepaired packet leaves frames undecodable until the next keyframe, so render
# rate is not checked here; sm_compare runs this scenario on libwebrtc for the comparison.
expect repair.fec_recovered > 100
expect video.residual_loss_pct < 1.5
expect net.fec_kbps > 0
